{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531664-v5-children-of-the-abyss-loresheet","id":1531664,"title":"V5 Children Of the Abyss Loresheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-27T20:16:01-08:00","id":1531664,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> V5 Children Of the Abyss Loresheet","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Children of the Abyss</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Lasombra Characters only)</span></div> <div align=\"center\">The Abyss always rewards a diligent student. The study of the Night Arts is often overlooked by<br /> the majority of Clan Lasombra, believing it to be a dangerous waste of time. The rare practitioners<br /> of Abyssal Mysticism are known as the Children of the Abyss, and they are rarely summoned to<br /> engage in the clan's political affairs. Whether out of fear or aversion, they are left to their own devices<br /> but never forgotten.<br /> They are typically employed as spies or assassins, and in rare cases where Clan Lasombra needs<br /> to make a point, weapons of mass destruction. These vampires are custodians of an age-old tradition<br /> rooted in their original and most formidable member\u2014the one who remained motionless in the<br /> depths of the deluge, communing with the Abyss as its first child: the progenitor of Clan Lasombra<br /> You are part of this tradition or have been initiated into this arduous journey. The whispers have<br /> reached your ears, whether through a Mawla or the darkness itself. Either way, you are a Child of<br /> the Dark, master and slave of the night.<br /> </div> <br /> \u25cf <b>Heart of Darkness</b>: The Children of the Abyss explore the fear of the dark as a weapon. In darkness, they become like gods, transforming ancestral fear into power. Their eyes see what others fear, enveloping everyone with the sense that true terror resides among the shadows. The Intimidation benefit granted by the Shadow Cloak ability affects Vampires. If you do not already possess the Shadow Cloak power, acquire it at no cost\u2014you may not necessarily have the discipline power, but rather a special variant of your own.<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf <b>Dive into the Tides of Oblivion</b>: As a Lasombra Clan vampire ages, a compulsion for the sea becomes increasingly present. When the vampire is submerged in saltwater, they can meditate, and by spending a point of Willpower, they can purify a stain caused by the influence of Oblivion on their Humanity track.<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b> Keeper of My Brothers</b>: Mystics are often overlooked for dedicating their lives to the tools they use, but their words carry weight and depth. You have Status (\u25cf) within the Lasombra clan. As a representative of your mentor within the order, you have received Mawla (\u25cf\u25cf). He holds a silent influence, aiding you in spiritual matters. This vampire can be added as a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>In the Shadow of the Legion</b>: As a member of one of the Lasombra clan's secret weapons, unlife has a slightly higher value than average, as long as it remains useful. By proving yourself truly worthy of the Lasombra clan, you have now gained the privilege to access the clan's martial elite for a story when needed. This benefit is available once per chronicle, and the number of members is linked to their importance to the clan. Each point of Status within Clan Lasombra allows you to summon a Legion member, or allows a additional use of this ability per chronicle. Each summoned legionnaire is equivalent to a Lethal Mortal (see in Vampire: The Masquerade, p. 185) with 8 dots in disciplines. Never forget that you are Lasombra, for the reckless misuse of this privilege is a direct invite to the Courts of Blood, where judgment awaits.<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b> Herald of the Abyss</b>: From the shadows emerges your deepest darkness. Each sacrifice is a step towards mastery. Now, at the apex, you can interfere, undo, or take control of any shadow conjured by another Oblivion user; completely stopping an attack or preventing someone from stepping into them requires a roll equal to your Resolve + Oblivion against a difficulty of 1 + the power level. Additionally concentration is no longer necessary for Oblivion powers, costing only as a minor action of three dice (see Minor Actions in Vampire: The Masquerade, p. 298) to conjure and command at the same turn. However, you can still only have one power that requires concentration active at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27426-nometao","name":"Nometao","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T07:12:44-08:00","id":1531683,"title":"","content":"Re #1, as written, this suggests you get the improved version of Shadow Cloak for free, which I don't think is intentionally. But even if you only get the &quot;normal&quot; version for free, it does sort of make the main power redundant, and for a lower cost.<br /> <br /> Usually, these abilities give you a limited version of the normal power for free (compare the Hecata power that gives you Obfuscate 1, but only against ghosts unless you have the normal version too) and then an improved version if you already have the original power.<br /> <br /> So it might just be a matter of switching the order a little and clarifying how the free version is less good than buying the &quot;base&quot; version, so it's:<br /> <br /> a. If you don't have Shadow Cloak already, gain a two-dice bonus to Intimidation against mortals, but not to Stealth. (Removing the Stealth bonus makes it less optimal than just buying Shadow Cloak in the first place.)<br /> <br /> b. If you already have Shadow Cloak, that power also works against Kindred. (This makes it so it's better to have this Loresheet and the power at the same time.)<br /> <br /> For #3, I'd switch around the bit about Influence and Mawla for sense, so:<br /> <br /> &quot;Gain Mawla (\u25cf\u25cf), representing a mentor within the order. Your mentor aids you in spiritual matters and may be added as a Touchstone if you wish. As a representative of your mentor, you also gain Status (\u25cf) within the Lasombra clan.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other than that, I really like this Loresheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T12:42:20-08:00","id":1531693,"title":"","content":"A good first attempt and wish you luck on further refinements on the lore sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}